    "body": "Hmm. So if in the future we wanted to make this work, we'd say to only throw if there is an entry in the registry with constructor equal to NewTarget/the active function object? I think that would work. So you'd break `new HTMLButtonElement` if you did `customElements.define(\"bad-1\", HTMLButtonElement)`, but if you don't do weird things then it could be fine.\n",
